// Defender advanced feature changed
//
// Fires when someone changes a Defender advanced feature in the portal. These are tenant-
// wide switches like tamper protection and EDR in block mode.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  Medium
// MITRE:     T1562.001
// Tables:    CloudAppEvents
// Custom details: Setting, NewValue
//
// Needs:
//   - The Defender for Cloud Apps Microsoft 365 connector with Microsoft 365 activities
//     turned on.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check which setting changed, the new value, who did it, and the ticket.
//   - Escalate if tamper protection, EDR in block mode or custom network indicators got
//     turned off, or Live Response unsigned scripts got turned on, with no ticket.
//   - Close if it's a ticketed change.
//
// Based on: Jeffrey Appel's post, https://jeffreyappel.nl/auditing-microsoft-defender-and-intune-configuration-changes/

CloudAppEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType == "SetAdvancedFeatures"
| extend Setting = tostring(RawEventData.SettingName), NewValue = tostring(RawEventData.SettingsNewValue)
| project Timestamp, ReportId, AccountObjectId, AccountDisplayName, IPAddress, Setting, NewValue
